ST patch order
==============

scripts/assemble-st.sh starts from the checked-in upstream ST 0.9.3 source,
verifies SHA256SUMS, and applies these patches in order:

1. st-alpha-20240814-a0274bc.diff
   https://st.suckless.org/patches/alpha/st-alpha-20240814-a0274bc.diff

2. st-scrollback-0.9.2.diff
   https://st.suckless.org/patches/scrollback/st-scrollback-0.9.2.diff

3. st-scrollback-selection-0.9.3.diff
   Local extension for this repository, applied after alpha and scrollback.
   Adds persistent selections, valid history bounds, mouse-wheel scrolling,
   and timer-driven selection scrolling at the top/bottom text row.
   It retains the 2,000-row history and does not introduce reflow.

The first two patches are unchanged upstream files. The third is maintained
alongside st/st.c, st/st.h, st/x.c, st/config.def.h and st/st.1. Assembly copies
the user's active config.h, then compares the generated implementation and
manual to the checked-in source so a forgotten patch update fails the build.

The local patch and SHA256SUMS must be refreshed together when changing the
selection implementation. No network access is needed for ST assembly.
